---
title: Connecting a hotel's own system (DEC-017)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor O as Hotel owner
    participant W as Website (host mode)
    participant A as Django API
    participant X as Hotel system (channel manager or PMS)
    participant J as Sync job
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    O->>W: Chooses "Connect my hotel system", enters system and access key
    W->>A: POST /host/integrations
    A->>X: test call with the key
    X-->>A: ok, property found
    A->>DB: save connection (key encrypted), status active
    A-)J: first import
    J->>X: read room types, prices, availability, services
    X-->>J: data
    J->>DB: create or update room types, nights, services (marked as imported)
    J->>DB: write sync log (what changed)
    A-->>W: connection active, rooms and services listed
    loop every 15 minutes
        J->>X: read changes
        J->>DB: update availability and prices
    end
    Note over A,X: a booking made on BLADUS lowers BLADUS availability at once and is sent to the hotel system when it accepts reservations
    Note over J,DB: if a sync fails, the last good data stays and the connection is flagged for the hotel and the admin
